# Environment Configuration Template

## Development

```bash
# .env.development
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=ai-treasure-hunt-dev
FIREBASE_API_KEY=YOUR_DEV_API_KEY
FIREBASE_APP_ID=YOUR_DEV_APP_ID
FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=YOUR_DEV_SENDER_ID
FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=YOUR_DEV_STORAGE_BUCKET

GEMINI_API_KEY=YOUR_GEMINI_API_KEY
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=YOUR_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY

APP_ENV=development
DEBUG_MODE=true
LOG_LEVEL=debug
ENABLE_ANALYTICS=true
ENABLE_NOTIFICATIONS=true
ENABLE_OFFLINE_MODE=false
```

## Staging

```bash
# .env.staging
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=ai-treasure-hunt-staging
FIREBASE_API_KEY=YOUR_STAGING_API_KEY
FIREBASE_APP_ID=YOUR_STAGING_APP_ID
FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=YOUR_STAGING_SENDER_ID
FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=YOUR_STAGING_STORAGE_BUCKET

GEMINI_API_KEY=YOUR_GEMINI_API_KEY_STAGING
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=YOUR_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY_STAGING

APP_ENV=staging
DEBUG_MODE=true
LOG_LEVEL=info
ENABLE_ANALYTICS=true
ENABLE_NOTIFICATIONS=true
ENABLE_OFFLINE_MODE=true
```

## Production

```bash
# .env.production
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=ai-treasure-hunt-prod
FIREBASE_API_KEY=YOUR_PROD_API_KEY
FIREBASE_APP_ID=YOUR_PROD_APP_ID
FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=YOUR_PROD_SENDER_ID
FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=YOUR_PROD_STORAGE_BUCKET

GEMINI_API_KEY=YOUR_GEMINI_API_KEY_PROD
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=YOUR_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY_PROD

APP_ENV=production
DEBUG_MODE=false
LOG_LEVEL=error
ENABLE_ANALYTICS=true
ENABLE_NOTIFICATIONS=true
ENABLE_OFFLINE_MODE=true
```

## How to Use

1. Copy this file and rename to `.env.development`, `.env.staging`, or `.env.production`
2. Replace `YOUR_*` with actual values
3. Add to `.gitignore` (never commit secrets)
4. Load in `main.dart` using `flutter_dotenv`

## Firebase Setup

### Get Firebase Credentials

1. Go to [Firebase Console](https://console.firebase.google.com/)
2. Select or create project
3. Go to Project Settings
4. Copy values from "Your apps" section

## API Keys

### Gemini API Key

1. Visit [Google AI Studio](https://makersuite.google.com/app/apikey)
2. Create API Key
3. Copy and paste

### Google Maps API Key

1. Go to [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/)
2. Create new project or select existing
3. Enable "Maps SDK for Android" and "Maps SDK for iOS"
4. Create API key in Credentials

## Security Notes

⚠️ **NEVER**:
- Commit `.env` files with real secrets
- Share API keys publicly
- Log sensitive data
- Use development keys in production

✅ **DO**:
- Keep secrets in environment variables
- Rotate keys regularly
- Use different keys per environment
- Store secrets in secure vaults (CI/CD)
